<p>3.3. ClearTax’s ability to perform its obligations is dependent on Customer fulfilling its obligations and, on any assumptions, set out in the Agreement or communicated by the Customer, being correct. To the extent that Customer does not fulfil its obligations under the Agreement or the agreed assumptions are, or become incorrect, then (without prejudice to our rights and remedies): (a) ClearTax shall be entitled to charge the Customer for its resources assigned to performing the Services even if not utilized, together with any additional charges which ClearTax incurs; (b) ClearTax may, at its sole and absolute discretion change the specification or scope of the Services or any agreed milestone dates and timetables; (c) ClearTax may revise the charges and the Customer agrees to accept changes to them; and (d) ClearTax shall be relieved of its obligations to the extent that it is prevented from fulfilling them in accordance with the Agreement.</p>
<p>3.4.The Customer’s availment of Services shall be subject to ClearTax Terms and Conditions of Use and Privacy Policy as updated from time to time by ClearTax.</p>
<p><strong>4.</strong> <strong>CHARGES AND PAYMENT</strong></p>
<p>4.1. <strong>Charges:</strong> The Customer shall pay the charges specified in Order Form. Except as otherwise specified herein or in an Order Form, (a) charges are based on the Services purchased and not on actual usage, unless specified otherwise in the Order Form and (b) payment obligations are non- cancellable, and charges paid are non-refundable.</p>
<p>4.2. <strong>Invoicing and Payment: </strong> Unless otherwise stated in the Order Form, all charges will be invoiced in advance and are payable within seven (7) days from the invoice date. The Customer shall be responsible for providing complete and accurate billing and contact information to ClearTax and notifying ClearTax of any changes to such information.</p>
<p>4.3.Unless otherwise stated in the Order Form, all invoices will be sent via email to the Customer’s email address registered with ClearTax.</p>
<p>4.4. Notwithstanding anything to the contrary, the Customer agrees that it shall not withhold any payments to be made to ClearTax or seek a waiver of its payment obligations, for any reason whatsoever.</p>
<p>4.5.<strong> Effect of Nonpayment:</strong> This agreement, Order Form, and Customer’s account (including all associated services, products and related agreements),hereinafter referred to as the "Entire Customer Account", may be suspended if any charges are not received by the invoice due date. Unpaid charges may be subject to interest at the lesser of two percent (2%) per month or the maximum permitted by Applicable Law, plus collection costs. Suspension of the Entire Customer Account will not relieve Customer’s obligation to pay charges due. Notwithstanding Clause 10.2, in the event of nonpayment, ClearTax may suspend the Entire Customer Account immediately upon the expiry of the invoice due date, without further notice or cure period.</p>
<p>4.6. <strong>Taxes: </strong> ClearTax’s charges do not include any taxes. The Customer shall be responsible for paying all taxes associated with its purchases hereunder.</p>
<p>4.7. The Customer shall, for every payment subject to Tax Deducted at Source ("TDS") under applicable Income Tax provisions, ensure that TDS is calculated, deducted, and deposited with the appropriate tax authorities in favor of ClearTax's PAN within the prescribed statutory time limits, and further, that the Customer provides ClearTax with the duly issued tax credit certificate in the form of Form 16A or its equivalent within the statutory period, such that the corresponding TDS credit is accurately reflected ClearTax's Form 26AS for the applicable financial year. In the event that ClearTax furnishes a valid certificate or notice from the relevant tax authority indicating a lower rate of tax deduction applicable to the payments made hereunder, the Customer shall comply with such certificate or notice and thereafter apply the lower rate. Should ClearTax, for any reason, be unable to claim credit for the TDS deducted (including, without limitation, any instance where such credit fails to be reflected in Form 26AS, or any refund claim is denied by the tax authorities), the Customer hereby agrees to reimburse or otherwise make whole ClearTax for any resultant shortfall or financial loss incurred, such reimbursement constituting the Customer’s irrevocable and enforceable obligation subject to ClearTax’s right to pursue any additional legal or equitable remedies available under this Agreement or applicable law.</p>
